{"title":"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The circumference of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb541f2dab7fcae7f600e13db3a6934d8fe1a13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\pi \\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. What is the radius of the circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e963b61aac0c03fa729c616f15ff180cbe863a43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20 \\text {cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 100 \\text {cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50 \\text {cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 25 \\text {cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 10 \\text {cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"512\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the circle. Using the equation for the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumference\" title=\"Circumference\">circumference</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/309a8d2dfb8fbbb877cfb81c98c24997d8ba3561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi r = C = 100\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52eac4736144e9503fe7658a5fde8bdda822da7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{100\\pi}{2\\pi} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 50 \\text {cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 CEMC Gauss (Gra